   "en": {
    "headline": "Google DeepMind unveils Genie 4, a world model that generates audio and can be edited with text in real time",
    "summary_short": "Google DeepMind launches Genie 4, which creates more realistic interactive worlds, with sound and lasting about two minutes. It targets film, games and robot training.",
    "summary_long": "Genie 4 is the new version of Google DeepMind's world model: it generates interactive scenes that the user explores in real time. It brings four new features: more realistic worlds, changes mid-experience with a text prompt, audio generation (music, ambient noise and dialogue) and support from Gemini 3.8 Flash in its simulations. Each experience lasts about two minutes, twice as long as with Genie 3. It will soon reach Google AI Ultra subscribers in Project Genie.\n\nGoogle pitches it for film pre-visualization, game prototyping and building training scenarios for robots. On Hacker News, with more than 500 comments, there was amazement and also criticism: physics errors and vanishing objects in the sample videos, controls that do not seem to respond and no technical details about the model.",
    "unconfirmed_claims": []
