   "en": {
    "headline": "Anthropic's IPO filing gives its seven cofounders 50.1% of the vote",
    "summary_short": "A single Class F share will give Anthropic's seven cofounders 50.1% of the vote after going public. The company presents it as protecting its mission; critics see a concentration of power.",
    "summary_long": "The S-1 that Anthropic filed to go public details who will run the company. Just before the offering it will issue a single Class F share, held by a company owned by its seven cofounders, including Dario and Daniela Amodei. That share will carry 50.1% of the votes, though not half of the ownership. In addition, Anthropic contributes 846 million shares, 5% of the total, to its own public benefit fund, and the cofounders pledge to donate 80% of their equity.\n\nThe company argues that the cofounders are best placed to steward its mission of safe AI against investor pressure, and that they will not run day-to-day operations. Commentator Matthew Berman sees it as a concentration of power over the future of AI. The filing also acknowledges catastrophic risks from advanced AI and that, according to Reuters, 47% of its 2025 sales went through Amazon and Google.",
    "unconfirmed_claims": [
     "The IPO will most likely take place in mid-November (according to midudev)."
    ]
   },
